{sov: Notes}
Hohner Clavinet D6 Climax: Built around multiple multi-tracked clavinet parts
panning across the mix in Eb Dorian / Eb Pentatonic.

Tuning & Key: Originally recorded on keyboard tuned to Eb minor. Guitarists
frequently tune down a half-step to Eb standard to play full open-string
percussive riffs, or stay in standard and use 6th-fret Ebm9/Ebm7 shell shapes.

Chorus Tension: The chorus steps out of the static Eb minor funk vamp with
explosive brass stabs moving between Bb7#9 and Cb7 (often played as B7 for ease).

Rhythm Function: Maintain a razor-sharp, percussive 16th-note scratch pattern.
Mute aggressively with the fretting hand to replicate the snappy key-release
decay of the Clavinet.
{eov}